1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:02,867
Pneumono, ultra, microscopic,
silico, volcano, coni,

2
00:00:02,867 --> 00:00:05,727
osis. Forty five letters.
Looks terrifying.

3
00:00:05,727 --> 00:00:11,448
Learn its few simple parts, and it
just means a lung disease

4
00:00:11,448 --> 00:00:13,354
from fine volcanic dust.

5
00:00:13,404 --> 00:00:16,779
This is MedLex. Make sense of
any medical word.

6
00:00:16,829 --> 00:00:19,492
Every medical word is a puzzle.

7
00:00:19,492 --> 00:00:23,488
Tap peri, card, and itis, and
pericarditis explains itself.

8
00:00:23,538 --> 00:00:25,805
Your day starts here. Ten minutes,

9
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:28,827
ten words, mixing new terms
with smart reviews.

10
00:00:28,877 --> 00:00:32,181
Quick rounds match each word
part to its meaning,

11
00:00:32,181 --> 00:00:34,016
so recall becomes second nature.

12
00:00:34,066 --> 00:00:37,018
Get it right, and MedLex shows you why.

13
00:00:37,018 --> 00:00:40,339
Gastr means stomach. Add itis, and
you have gastritis.

14
00:00:40,389 --> 00:00:42,983
Then flip it around. Build
the word yourself,

15
00:00:42,983 --> 00:00:44,930
from the pieces you now know.

16
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:48,101
Every term in the library is taken apart,

17
00:00:48,101 --> 00:00:50,833
explained in plain words,
and spoken aloud.

18
00:00:50,883 --> 00:00:54,750
Sixty six prefixes, sixty roots,
and a hundred suffixes.

19
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:57,329
Learn them once, and decode thousands.

20
00:00:57,379 --> 00:01:01,411
Fourteen hundred and eighty terms.
Twenty six modules.

21
00:01:01,411 --> 00:01:03,427
Fifty six illustrated guides.

22
00:01:03,545 --> 00:01:07,563
The Visual Atlas turns tricky
ideas into beautiful,

23
00:01:07,563 --> 00:01:08,568
illustrated guides.

24
00:01:08,618 --> 00:01:12,628
Lessons walk you through each body
system on a single,

25
00:01:12,628 --> 00:01:13,430
beautiful canvas.

26
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,523
Every module comes with clear outcomes,

27
00:01:15,523 --> 00:01:18,247
so you always know what you have mastered.

28
00:01:18,297 --> 00:01:20,025
And when you have five minutes,

29
00:01:20,025 --> 00:01:22,329
eight kinds of practice keep it all fresh.

30
00:01:22,509 --> 00:01:25,945
Words make more sense when you
know their story.

31
00:01:25,945 --> 00:01:30,145
Travel nine eras, from ancient Egypt to
Vesalius and the Fabrica.

32
00:01:30,195 --> 00:01:33,850
Every root gets a memory
picture and a hook.

33
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:36,286
Card means heart. Add tachy, fast,

34
00:01:36,286 --> 00:01:39,128
and tachycardia is an
abnormally fast heartbeat.

35
00:01:39,178 --> 00:01:42,958
Hemi means half. So hemiplegia is
paralysis of one half,

36
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:45,225
one side, of the body. Listen,

37
00:01:45,225 --> 00:01:47,115
and say it out loud.

38
00:01:47,165 --> 00:01:50,159
Then prove it stuck. A quick
check after each card,

39
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:52,853
with points the first time
you get it right.

40
00:01:52,903 --> 00:01:55,316
Sixty roots, grouped by body system.

41
00:01:55,316 --> 00:01:59,338
Watch your mastery grow, and unlock
achievements on the way.

42
00:01:59,388 --> 00:02:00,310
Open MedLex free, and decode
your first word today.

